# Import link inside a code fence

`BUGS.md` `v2-native-front-in-fence-imports-not-followed`. The Markdown link form
`[names](path.ssc)` is an import wherever it stands — the same statement above the
fence and inside it must load the same module.

The native lane's import scanner used to flip into "skip to the closing fence" mode
on the opening ` ``` `, so an in-fence link was never collected and every imported
name stayed unbound. `v1` resolved it fine, which made this a pure lane divergence:
`bin/ssc run` printed `ssc: unbound global: square` for this exact program while
`ssc-tools run --v1` printed the numbers below.

```scalascript
[square, cube, factorial](./lib/math-utils.ssc)
println(square(5))
println(cube(3))
println(factorial(6))
```

The second fence checks that a *later* fence still sees the module imported by the
first — the scan is over the whole document, not per fence.

```scalascript
println(square(7))
```
